From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: media: i2c: vd55g: Honour st,leds only with vd55g.illuminator=1

The romulus13 device tree now names sensor GPIO 1 as the strobe output
(st,leds = <1>, the pin Windows writes 0x0468 = 0x02 on), so that the IR
emitter stage C can test whether the strobe signal enables the emitter path.
Patch 0041 made the property the only way to get a strobe GPIO and the
led_mode control, which would now be on for every boot. Make it opt-in a
second time: a read-only module parameter illuminator (default 0). Without it
st,leds is read and ignored (one log line) and the driver behaves exactly as
without the property: every GPIO an input, no flash LED mode control.

The omarchy-surface-sl7 modprobe rule sets illuminator=1 on the "linux-sl7
(IR test)" boot entry (sl7.ir_test=1 on the command line) and nowhere else, so
a normal boot never drives GPIO 1.

The GPIO configuration is latched when the stream starts
(vd55g_update_gpios() in vd55g_enable_streams()), so user space must set
led_mode before the stream is started; a change while streaming is written at
once. Documented in the comment above the parameter.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
index 761e6d1a86d2..73ccf6a165d1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
@@ -2001,6 +2001,24 @@ static int vd55g_parse_dt_gpios_array(struct vd55g *sensor, char *prop_name,
 	return 0;
 }

+/*
+ * SL7 local: the infrared illuminator strobe is opt-in. The DT of the Surface
+ * Laptop 7 carries 'st,leds = <1>' (sensor GPIO 1 is the strobe output), but
+ * the driver honours it only with illuminator=1, which the omarchy-surface-sl7
+ * modprobe rule sets on the "linux-sl7 (IR test)" boot entry alone. Without it
+ * the property is ignored: no GPIO is a strobe output and the flash LED mode
+ * control is not created, exactly as without the property (patch 0041).
+ *
+ * The GPIO configuration is latched at stream start (vd55g_update_gpios() in
+ * vd55g_enable_streams()), so set the led_mode control before the stream is
+ * started. A change while streaming is written at once, but start-up
+ * ordering is what the IR emitter test relies on.
+ */
+static bool illuminator;
+module_param(illuminator, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(illuminator,
+		 "SL7 local: honour the st,leds strobe GPIO and expose the led_mode control (default off; set only by the sl7.ir_test=1 modprobe gate)");
+
 static int vd55g_parse_dt_gpios(struct vd55g *sensor)
 {
 	u32 led_gpios[VD55G_NB_GPIOS];
@@ -2019,6 +2037,15 @@ static int vd55g_parse_dt_gpios(struct vd55g *sensor)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

+	if (nb_gpios_leds && !illuminator) {
+		dev_info(sensor->dev,
+			 "st,leds ignored: illuminator=0 (IR test boot only)\n");
+		nb_gpios_leds = 0;
+	} else if (nb_gpios_leds) {
+		dev_warn(sensor->dev,
+			 "illuminator=1: strobe GPIO output and led_mode control enabled\n");
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < nb_gpios_leds; i++) {
 		sensor->gpios[led_gpios[i]] = VD55G_GPIO_MODE_STROBE;
 		set_bit(led_gpios[i], &sensor->ext_leds_mask);
